# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# OpenClawd Agent Kit — environment template
#
# Copy to `.env` and fill in what you use. NEVER commit `.env` — the repo
# .gitignore already excludes it. Every variable here is optional; the kit
# fails closed (gate escalates, MCP stays read-only, loop stays dry-run)
# when the pieces it needs are missing.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# ── Jev gate (kit-core) ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# TypeSafe API key. The Jev gate reads ONLY this variable — never files or
# flags. Without it, consequential tool calls escalate to a human (and the
# default approver denies).
# https://typesafe.ai
TYPESAFE_API_KEY=

# ── Solana (kit-solana) ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Solana RPC endpoint. A private endpoint (Helius, QuikNode, Triton) is
# strongly recommended; the public mainnet endpoint is the fallback.
SOLANA_RPC_URL=https://api.mainnet-beta.solana.com

# Local signer (feature: local-signer) — the original kit's custody flow,
# kept for parity. The kit's default flows are unsigned / remote-signed and
# never read this. Dev only; NEVER commit a real value.
# SOLANA_PRIVATE_KEY=

# Remote signer (kit-solana::RemoteSigner) — an operator-run signing
# endpoint, plus its optional bearer token.
# KIT_REMOTE_SIGNER_URL=https://signer.example.internal/sign
# KIT_REMOTE_SIGNER_TOKEN=

# ── MCP (kit-mcp) ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Fleet MCP servers. Defaults are the production endpoints; override for
# staging or local mirrors.
# CLAWD_COMPUTE_MCP_URL=https://mcp.clawdcompute.us/mcp
# PUMPAI_MCP_URL=https://pumpai.ai/mcp

# ── EVM / cross-chain (kit-evm) ──────────────────────────────────────────────

# EVM-compatible RPC endpoint (e.g. Arbitrum, Base, Ethereum mainnet).
# ETHEREUM_RPC_URL=https://arb1.arbitrum.io/rpc

# Hex private key (0x-prefixed) for the opt-in local EVM signer.
# ETHEREUM_PRIVATE_KEY=0x...

# ── HTTP service (kit-http) ──────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Set to 1 to let the HTTP service execute gate-cleared consequential calls
# instead of simulating them. Leave unset for the safe dry-run default.
# KIT_HTTP_LIVE=

# ── Clawd constitution overrides (optional) ──────────────────────────────────

# The kit auto-discovers an installed constitution (~/.clawd/, ./constitution/)
# and otherwise uses the byte-for-byte inline fallback.
# CLAWD_CONSTITUTION_PATH=/abs/path/to/constitution.md

# ── Logging ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Optional. Controls verbosity: error | warn | info | debug | trace
# RUST_LOG=info
